  id:"gibbonriver", name:"Gibbon River", color:"#3f7f4f",
  state:"WY", region:"yellowstone", gauges:["gibbonMadJct"], primaryGauge:"gibbonMadJct",
  geom:"nhd",   // NHD linework clipped to the park boundary — don't re-snap
  parkRegs:"Below Gibbon Falls it is <b>fly fishing only</b> and part of the Nonnative Trout Tolerance Area — keep up to five brook trout, release rainbows and browns. Opens <b>May 1</b> — the Firehole, the Gibbon below the Grand Loop Road bridge near the Museum of the National Park Ranger, the Madison, and the associated tributaries of each open a month ahead of the rest of the park.",
  goodFlow:null, // TODO: set {min:___,max:___} (CFS) for YOUR good-flow range on this river
  blurb:"Out of Grebe and Wolf lakes, through Norris and the Gibbon Meadows, over Gibbon Falls and down the canyon to Madison Junction. Two rivers in one: small meadow and pocket water above the falls, a bigger, warmer river below it.",
  fish:"Brook trout and grayling in the upper meadows, browns and rainbows below the falls. The meadow reaches are small-stream fishing — short casts, a low profile, and elk in the willows.",
